INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(27,'atlanta',0,'# Overall statistics and changes in population ## Demographic information ## City-specific information about homelessness based on city''s context ## Contributing factors ## Income # City government policies # City-specific resources ## Shelters, temporary housing, housing programs for long term residency ## Biggest local non-profits ## Healthcare and mental health ### Primary care ### Emergency ### Mental health ### Addiction ### Other ## Education and training ### Continuing Education ### Job training and employment programs ## Post-Incarceration Resources ## Veterans Resources # Sources # City: Atlanta, GA # Scope: Homelessness context and resources # Timeframe: Data primarily from 2016–2024 (city and state context) ## Summary (High-level) - In 2024, Atlanta counted 2,867 people experiencing homelessness across 243 neighborhoods, with about 1,827 sheltered and 1,040 unsheltered. - Overall homelessness is down 30% since 2016, but rose 7% in the last year, driven by a 41% jump in unsheltered homelessness and increases in some subpopulations.','[0.01837158203125,-0.050537109375,0.01390838623046875,0.02862548828125,0.0811767578125,0.0645751953125,0.0755615234375,0.036224365234375,-0.005405426025390625,-0.042205810546875,-0.04486083984375,-0.01934814453125,-0.09326171875,0.0175933837890625,-0.0289459228515625,0.062408447265625,0.061920166015625,-0.03826904296875,0.018280029296875,-0.0000654458999633789,0.0183258056640625,0.033538818359375,0.0269775390625,0.052276611328125,0.0213623046875,-0.00974273681640625,0.00630950927734375,-0.033294677734375,-0.07464599609375,0.01393890380859375,-0.011016845703125,-0.004367828369140625,0.012969970703125,-0.00626373291015625,0.029754638671875,-0.0041351318359375,-0.004119873046875,-0.017913818359375,0.016143798828125,0.0113525390625,-0.044097900390625,-0.006732940673828125,0.01293182373046875,-0.0087432861328125,-0.03619384765625,-0.049072265625,0.0177459716796875,0.0187225341796875,0