INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(28,'atlanta',1,'827 sheltered and 1,040 unsheltered. - Overall homelessness is down 30% since 2016, but rose 7% in the last year, driven by a 41% jump in unsheltered homelessness and increases in some subpopulations. - High rates of mental illness, substance use, disability, trauma, and extreme housing costs drive needs; housing-focused strategies and supportive programs are central to the response. --- ## Overall statistics and trends ### Population level and trends - FACT: Overall homeless population - City: Atlanta - Topic: population_trend - Content: In 2024, Atlanta counted 2,867 people experiencing homelessness. This is a 7% increase from 2023, but a 30% decrease since the first PIT Count in 2016. - FACT: Sheltered vs unsheltered - City: Atlanta - Topic: unsheltered_vs_sheltered - Content: Of the 2,867 people in 2024, 1,223 were in emergency shelter, 604 in transitional housing, and 1,040 were unsheltered. Unsheltered homelessness increased by about 41% compared to the prior year. - FACT: Families vs individuals (recent trends) - City: Atlanta - Topic: population_trend_household_type - Content: Recent PIT data show a 22% decrease in adults with children experiencing homelessness since earlier years. In 2024, there were 115 homeless families, with most in emergency shelters and a few unsheltered.','[0.027587890625,-0.036865234375,0.00008475780487060547,0.00266265869140625,0.0821533203125,0.037506103515625,0.06494140625,0.05499267578125,-0.01415252685546875,-0.026092529296875,-0.0457763671875,-0.03472900390625,-0.07318115234375,0.0200347900390625,0.0199127197265625,0.05621337890625,0.09521484375,-0.0217742919921875,-0.00972747802734375,0.0015268325805664062,0.053680419921875,-0.00310516357421875,0.004184722900390625,0.0124664306640625,0.037139892578125,-0.0203857421875,0.04779052734375,-0.048553466796875,-0.0709228515625,-0.0079345703125,0.004520416259765625,0.0220794677734375,-0.007015228271484375,-0.01513671875,0.0297698974609375