INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(31,'atlanta',4,'pic: demographics_gender_veterans - Content: Men make up about 91% of homeless veterans in the Atlanta CoC. Women represent about 8%, and around 1% identify with a culturally specific gender identity. --- ## Contributing factors and structural context - FACT: Housing market pressures (regional) - Topic: contributing_factors_housing - Content: Atlanta faces rapid growth, rising rents, and low vacancy rates. These conditions make it hard to prevent people from entering homelessness and threaten recent gains without sustained investment. - FACT: Mental health care and statewide context - Topic: contributing_factors_health_system - Content: Georgia ranks among the worst states for access to mental health services. Limited treatment options intersect with high rates of serious mental illness and substance use among people experiencing homelessness. - FACT: Affordable housing shortage (state context) - Topic: contributing_factors_affordable_units - Content: In Georgia, there are only about 34 affordable rental units for every 100 low‑income households. This shortage pushes many families into unstable housing or homelessness. - FACT: Education system impact - Topic: contributing_factors_schools - Content: About 4% of Atlanta Public Schools students experienced homelessness in the last year.','[0.038665771484375,-0.0204315185546875,-0.0135345458984375,0.037322998046875,0.05462646484375,0.07275390625,0.076904296875,0.051361083984375,-0.0167388916015625,-0.01473236083984375,-0.07171630859375,-0.00788116455078125,-0.07220458984375,0.033935546875,-0.059478759765625,0.06805419921875,0.06231689453125,-0.0286865234375,0.034027099609375,0.003818511962890625,0.02801513671875,0.0533447265625,0.01233673095703125,0.042633056640625,0.030517578125,0.0033740997314453125,0.025726318359375,-0.0185089111328125,-0.052032470703125,0.002712249755859375,0.0018835067749023438,-0.027252197265625,-0.006557464599609375,-0.01373291015625,0.02914428710937