INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(32,'atlanta',5,'nstable housing or homelessness. - FACT: Education system impact - Topic: contributing_factors_schools - Content: About 4% of Atlanta Public Schools students experienced homelessness in the last year. This shows how housing instability touches many children and families beyond those counted in adult-focused systems. --- ## Subpopulations and local patterns ### Subpopulations (PIT-defined) - FACT: Families - City: Atlanta - Topic: subpopulation_families - Content: In 2024, 115 homeless families were counted: 80 in emergency shelter, 29 in transitional housing, and 6 unsheltered. Family homelessness has decreased compared with prior years, helped by prevention and rapid exit strategies. - FACT: Youth (18–24) - City: Atlanta - Topic: subpopulation_youth - Content: In 2024, 188 youth were counted: 115 in emergency shelter, 39 in transitional housing, and 34 unsheltered. Youth homelessness has recently increased, prompting targeted outreach and housing solutions for unaccompanied and parenting youth. - FACT: Veterans - City: Atlanta - Topic: subpopulation_veterans - Content: In 2024, there were 287 homeless veterans: 115 in transitional housing, 82 in emergency shelter, and 101 unsheltered. Veteran homelessness rose but less than other groups, and plans prioritize housing and VA‑linked services.','[0.010498046875,-0.03460693359375,0.0284271240234375,0.0121307373046875,0.06695556640625,0.0283203125,0.0860595703125,0.056060791015625,-0.044036865234375,-0.0433349609375,-0.05615234375,-0.02386474609375,-0.04986572265625,0.02508544921875,-0.0135498046875,0.036163330078125,0.07611083984375,-0.02471923828125,0.02703857421875,-0.00444793701171875,0.01142120361328125,0.017608642578125,0.004673004150390625,0.03033447265625,0.0230712890625,-0.006862640380859375,0.021209716796875,-0.036956787109375,-0.058380126953125,0.006313323974609375,-0.011444091796875,-0.006977081298828125,-0.0184478759765625,-0.010955810546875,0.037445068359375,0.