INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(33,'atlanta',6,'homeless veterans: 115 in transitional housing, 82 in emergency shelter, and 101 unsheltered. Veteran homelessness rose but less than other groups, and plans prioritize housing and VA‑linked services. ### Trauma, health, and experiences (Atlanta Mission data) - FACT: Trauma and violence - Topic: life_experiences_trauma - Content: Among Atlanta Mission clients, 81% have experienced physical or sexual abuse and 58% report trauma symptoms. Many grew up with unhealthy relationships and unresolved traumatic events. - FACT: Health conditions - Topic: life_experiences_health - Content: About 57% of clients report a chronic medical condition. Many also live with serious mental illness, substance use history, or disability, making stable housing and care coordination critical. - FACT: Social isolation and employment - Topic: life_experiences_social_economic - Content: More than half of Atlanta Mission clients say they usually spend free time alone, and around 46% are under‑ or unemployed. This isolation and unstable work complicate recovery and housing stability. - FACT: Substance use - Topic: life_experiences_substance_use - Content: About 30–40% of adults served report drug or alcohol abuse, and many have serious mental illness. This aligns with national estimates but shows that most people experiencing homelessness are not primarily defined by addiction.','[0.03509521484375,0.0107879638671875,-0.0133514404296875,0.0028533935546875,0.06512451171875,0.04571533203125,0.10479736328125,0.041290283203125,-0.0199432373046875,-0.0167694091796875,-0.050750732421875,0.01751708984375,-0.059661865234375,0.01010894775390625,0.028167724609375,0.05938720703125,0.09600830078125,-0.01485443115234375,0.0244140625,-0.01262664794921875,0.0220489501953125,0.01436614990234375,0.00537109375,0.0377197265625,0.031890869140625,-0.026580810546875,0.02398681640625,-0.04974365234375,-0.04913330078125,0.021148681640625,0.005687713623046875,-0.018737792968