INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(34,'atlanta',7,'ved report drug or alcohol abuse, and many have serious mental illness. This aligns with national estimates but shows that most people experiencing homelessness are not primarily defined by addiction. - FACT: Statewide veterans and poverty - Topic: state_context_veterans - Content: Across Georgia, about 40,000 veterans live in poverty, and more than 600 experience homelessness. This gives context to the veteran homelessness seen in Atlanta’s local counts. --- ## Preferences, barriers, and service system ### Barriers to shelter and housing (PIT supplemental) - FACT: Shelter preferences and safety - Topic: barriers_shelter_safety - Content: In an unsheltered survey, 61% said they would use shelter if available, 34% would not, and 5% were unsure. Major deterrents included safety concerns, crowding, bed bugs, strict rules, and lack of privacy. - FACT: Preference for outdoor living - Topic: barriers_shelter_preference - Content: Some unsheltered people prefer to live outdoors rather than in traditional shelters. Reasons include mental health issues, discomfort with rules, and feeling safer or more in control outside. - FACT: Documentation and eligibility - Topic: barriers_documentation - Content: A small share of unsheltered people cannot qualify for housing programs because of missing documents like Social Security IDs or birth certificates.','[0.033538818359375,0.005825042724609375,-0.01068115234375,0.0183563232421875,0.08746337890625,0.04608154296875,0.088134765625,0.016326904296875,-0.0164794921875,-0.035858154296875,-0.04840087890625,0.00780487060546875,-0.068115234375,0.0279998779296875,-0.0181427001953125,0.078125,0.0889892578125,0.02032470703125,0.018463134765625,-0.0070037841796875,0.05120849609375,0.006671905517578125,0.01044464111328125,0.034576416015625,0.0234832763671875,-0.0027332305908203125,0.033905029296875,-0.035552978515625,-0.050811767578125,0.01030731201171875,-0.0029201507568359375,-0.01068878173828125,