INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(35,'atlanta',8,'gibility - Topic: barriers_documentation - Content: A small share of unsheltered people cannot qualify for housing programs because of missing documents like Social Security IDs or birth certificates. These documentation gaps block access to housing resources. - FACT: Paths from street to housing - Topic: housing_pathways_unsheltered - Content: Recent encampment work shows many unsheltered neighbors want to move directly from the street into housing, often preferring non‑congregate, private settings. In 2023, only 11% moved directly; most went through shelter first. - FACT: Income and benefits (unsheltered) - Topic: income_unsheltered - Content: About 61% of the unsheltered population reported no income. Only 7% reported earned income, and around 72% said they received no benefits; among those with benefits, SNAP was the most common. ### Health access - FACT: Disability and treatment gaps - Topic: health_disability_treatment - Content: About 67% of surveyed people reported a disability, but only 37% were receiving treatment. This reveals major gaps between health needs and actual care for people experiencing homelessness. - FACT: Health insurance - Topic: health_insurance - Content: Nearly 60% of surveyed respondents lacked health insurance. Among those insured, most were covered by Medicaid or Medicare, showing dependence on public programs for care.','[0.0443115234375,-0.01444244384765625,-0.004817962646484375,0.030731201171875,0.08001708984375,0.034332275390625,0.0771484375,0.038299560546875,-0.016937255859375,-0.040008544921875,-0.015045166015625,-0.019195556640625,-0.0552978515625,0.01491546630859375,0.0101776123046875,0.05841064453125,0.087646484375,0.0300445556640625,-0.046112060546875,0.037506103515625,0.03662109375,-0.0067901611328125,-0.01129913330078125,0.0109100341796875,0.041534423828125,0.01331329345703125,0.048248291015625,-0.034027099609375,-0.06256103515625,-0.0026531219482421875,0.01108551025390625,-0.