INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(36,'atlanta',9,'health_insurance - Content: Nearly 60% of surveyed respondents lacked health insurance. Among those insured, most were covered by Medicaid or Medicare, showing dependence on public programs for care. --- ## Local programs and interventions ### Housing-focused strategies (Partners for Home) - FACT: Housing as central solution - Topic: housing_strategy_core - Content: Stimulus funds allowed Atlanta to test rehousing strategies that sped up exits and stabilized lives. Housing with supports is the core solution, and the system has used this model to reduce homelessness since 2016. - FACT: Housing pipeline - Topic: housing_pipeline - Content: Atlanta is investing in more than 1,100 housing units dedicated to people exiting homelessness. These units are designed near resources like food, transport, and jobs, aiming to support long‑term stability. - FACT: Risk from funding loss - Topic: housing_funding_risk - Content: Leaders warn that without sustained funding similar to prior stimulus, gains are at risk. Rising rents and low vacancy could outpace current capacity to prevent and resolve homelessness.','[0.0198211669921875,-0.059326171875,0.016357421875,0.0413818359375,0.0845947265625,0.06732177734375,0.046142578125,0.03692626953125,-0.0257568359375,-0.06622314453125,0.004093170166015625,-0.0080718994140625,-0.04644775390625,0.0079803466796875,-0.0005636215209960938,0.03692626953125,0.07196044921875,-0.00229644775390625,-0.0003864765167236328,0.024322509765625,0.0243682861328125,0.036163330078125,0.006561279296875,0.04241943359375,0.0316162109375,-0.0357666015625,0.015228271484375,-0.01427459716796875,-0.050048828125,-0.01245880126953125,0.02008056640625,-0.01071929931640625,0.0192413330078125,-0.022979736328125,0.03558349609375,0.020538330078125,-0.0126495361328125,0.008758544921875,0.00750732421875,0.0142974853515625,-0.061737060546875,0.0177154541015625,-0.03778076171875,-0.0017652511596679688,-0.03924560546875,0.0017528533