INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(38,'atlanta',11,'Desire for change and work - Topic: services_motivation - Content: Atlanta Mission reports hundreds of people completing needs assessments, progressing through programs, and ending their homelessness. Many clients actively seek work and stability when given support and opportunities. - FACT: Employment supports - Topic: services_employment - Content: Through a partnership with Cara and its Next Steps vocational program, Atlanta Mission offers job training and placement. Many graduates achieve stable employment, though transportation, clothing, and ID remain barriers. - FACT: Women and children in shelters - Topic: services_women_children - Content: Nearly 4,000 women and children sought shelter at Atlanta Mission last year. Programs like My Sister’s House and the new Restoration House focus specifically on women and children’s safety, stability, and long‑term change. - FACT: Shelter as transformation, not “enabling” - Topic: services_model - Content: Atlanta Mission’s model aims to address root causes like trauma and unhealthy relationships, not just provide beds. Staff work with clients to build independence and break cycles of poverty and homelessness.','[0.042877197265625,-0.0283355712890625,0.0029277801513671875,-0.0118408203125,0.07794189453125,0.060455322265625,0.07391357421875,0.047607421875,-0.0228729248046875,-0.04425048828125,-0.0465087890625,0.0284271240234375,-0.045196533203125,0.01629638671875,0.002620697021484375,0.043975830078125,0.082763671875,-0.0002639293670654297,0.024871826171875,0.01153564453125,0.001140594482421875,0.043304443359375,0.00366973876953125,0.0299530029296875,0.031036376953125,-0.02362060546875,-0.003414154052734375,-0.054718017578125,-0.050811767578125,-0.0012340545654296875,0.0306854248046875,-0.040740966796875,0.022674560546875,-0.00524139404296875,0.00977325439453125,-0.00855255126953125,0.01085662841796875,0.005615234375,0.0222930908203125,-0.0279693603515625,-0.034515380859375,-0