INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(39,'boston',0,'# City: Boston, MA # Scope: Homelessness context and resources # Timeframe: Data primarily from 2021–2025 (Greater Boston and statewide context included) ## Summary (High-level) - Boston’s total homeless count fell 4.3% from 2024 to 2025, after several years of post‑pandemic increases and system strain. - Most people are sheltered; Boston has one of the lowest unsheltered rates among major U.S. cities, but regional homelessness has risen. - Families, children, migrants, and people of color face the sharpest pressures in a very tight, expensive housing market with complex, time‑limited supports. --- ## Overall statistics and trends ### Population level and trends - FACT: Overall homeless population - City: Boston - Topic: population_trend - Content: From 2024 to 2025, Boston’s homeless count fell 5,756→5,506 (–4.3%). Adults increased 2,036→2,122 (+4.2%). People in families fell 3,720→3,384 (–9%). - FACT: Unsheltered vs sheltered - City: Boston - Topic: unsheltered_vs_sheltered - Content: In 2025, 132 adults were unsheltered (slightly fewer than 2024), and no families were unsheltered, as since 2007. About 2.4% of Boston’s homeless population was unsheltered.','[0.039520263671875,-0.04486083984375,0.03961181640625,-0.018341064453125,0.061859130859375,0.01169586181640625,0.073486328125,0.07666015625,-0.0200347900390625,-0.045318603515625,-0.06671142578125,-0.039642333984375,-0.06524658203125,0.01776123046875,-0.0031032562255859375,0.051177978515625,0.0977783203125,-0.030914306640625,-0.005992889404296875,-0.00780487060546875,0.04278564453125,-0.0163421630859375,0.0204315185546875,0.032440185546875,0.03277587890625,-0.010528564453125,0.034088134765625,-0.02117919921875,-0.07220458984375,-0.0277252197265625,0.012451171875,0.0068206787109375,-0.027862548828125,-0.0305328369140625,0.043212890625,0.0005269050598144531,-0.0218048095703125,0.00984954833984375,-0.01218414306640625,0.0229644775390625,-0.028656005859375,-0.0118103027