INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(40,'boston',1,'ed_vs_sheltered - Content: In 2025, 132 adults were unsheltered (slightly fewer than 2024), and no families were unsheltered, as since 2007. About 2.4% of Boston’s homeless population was unsheltered. - FACT: State and regional trends - City: Greater Boston / Massachusetts - Topic: population_trend_regional - Content: Massachusetts has seen one of the largest recent homelessness increases, above the U.S. 18% rise. In Greater Boston, nearly all 2023–2024 growth came from people in families, often outside Boston. ### Demographic patterns - FACT: Race and ethnicity - Topic: demographics_race - Content: In Greater Boston, Black residents experience homelessness at about 17× the rate of White residents, and Latino residents at about 5×. These racial disparities have recently worsened. - FACT: Age groups - Topic: demographics_age - Content: In Greater Boston, homelessness among youth under 18 rose roughly 72% from 2023–2024. In Boston, unaccompanied youth (up to 24) decreased slightly 132→128, with almost all staying in shelters or programs. - FACT: Migrants and new arrivals - Topic: demographics_migrants - Content: In about two years, more than 20,000 migrants, many from Haiti and Central/South America and some fleeing gang violence, have arrived in MA. Many depend on shelters or unstable, overcrowded, or unsafe housing.','[0.04248046875,-0.03839111328125,0.01715087890625,-0.00537109375,0.0714111328125,0.0196533203125,0.049774169921875,0.0625,-0.0225067138671875,-0.043212890625,-0.06341552734375,-0.037994384765625,-0.07049560546875,0.02606201171875,0.01068878173828125,0.06103515625,0.08905029296875,-0.02880859375,-0.0188446044921875,0.009033203125,0.057403564453125,-0.0250244140625,0.0214996337890625,0.016448974609375,0.02557373046875,-0.0182952880859375,0.033721923828125,-0.0294036865234375,-0.07061767578125,-0.02301025390625,0.0244903564453125,-0.0016088485717773438,-0.0181884765625,-0.021148681640625,0.048187255859375,0.00