INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(43,'boston',4,'olitical instability, or economic collapse and then face MA’s severe housing shortage. They confront sky‑high rents, few vacancies, language barriers, and limited access to permanent affordable units. - PATHWAY: School-connected family homelessness - Applies to: Families with children in Boston Public Schools - Content: Groups serving Boston Public Schools families report long lists of households couch‑surfing, in cars, facing eviction, or losing shelter beds. Many wait months or years for vouchers or affordable units to become available. - PATHWAY: Administrative and timing failures in housing programs - Applies to: Families using state assistance (e.g., HomeBase) - Content: Some families lose apartments when subsidy approvals, like HomeBase funds, arrive too late. Even after finding a willing landlord, slow processing or bureaucratic delays can cause units to be rented to others instead. ### Barriers to exiting homelessness - BARRIER: Lack of affordable units - Applies to: Most single adults and families - Content: There are far fewer affordable units than households that need them. Waitlists for public and subsidized housing can last many years or even decades, so families can remain in shelter or unstable situations for long periods.','[0.00884246826171875,-0.020111083984375,0.0224761962890625,0.007740020751953125,0.06439208984375,0.0222625732421875,0.041229248046875,0.054962158203125,-0.028656005859375,-0.07183837890625,-0.048248291015625,-0.02093505859375,-0.041290283203125,0.049835205078125,0.00395965576171875,0.0198974609375,0.0814208984375,-0.01800537109375,-0.0169525146484375,-0.007587432861328125,0.033447265625,0.0133056640625,-0.01236724853515625,0.032745361328125,0.03375244140625,-0.020477294921875,0.0018939971923828125,-0.009918212890625,-0.068359375,-0.034088134765625,0.02947998046875,-0.026458740234375,-0.0246734619140625,-0.0037517547607421875,0.03460693359375,-0.0018596649169921875,0.0033721923828125,0.