INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(44,'boston',5,'rdable units than households that need them. Waitlists for public and subsidized housing can last many years or even decades, so families can remain in shelter or unstable situations for long periods. - BARRIER: System at “breaking point” - Applies to: Families and individuals seeking help - Content: Providers describe the shelter and housing aid system as overwhelmed. Shelters are full, caseloads are huge, and groups that once placed nearly every family now routinely turn people away because no beds or units are available. - BARRIER: Policy limits and time pressure in shelters - Applies to: Families in state-run shelters - Content: Nine‑month stay limits compress the time families have to secure housing, even though it often takes a year or more. Caseworkers sometimes have only weeks to find units, raising the risk of exits from shelter into street homelessness. - BARRIER: Documentation and bureaucratic complexity - Applies to: Low-income residents and migrants - Content: Vouchers and affordable housing require detailed housing histories, IDs, credit records, and precise paperwork. Language gaps, missing documents, or small errors can derail applications, making the system feel impossible to navigate.','[-0.01041412353515625,-0.00963592529296875,-0.0020465850830078125,-0.0107269287109375,0.0675048828125,0.0307159423828125,0.03997802734375,0.0062713623046875,-0.0277862548828125,-0.05731201171875,-0.01131439208984375,-0.0118408203125,-0.01308441162109375,0.036834716796875,-0.007328033447265625,0.032073974609375,0.055450439453125,-0.001140594482421875,-0.0014944076538085938,-0.0220489501953125,0.032073974609375,0.0130767822265625,-0.01216888427734375,0.008453369140625,0.040557861328125,-0.016387939453125,0.0223541259765625,-0.031097412109375,-0.048797607421875,-0.0144195556640625,0.039825439453125,-0.039031982421875,-0.057708740234375,-0.01256561279296875,0.0107574462890625,-0.0235137939453125,-0.0384521484375,-0.014144897