INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(45,'boston',6,'equire detailed housing histories, IDs, credit records, and precise paperwork. Language gaps, missing documents, or small errors can derail applications, making the system feel impossible to navigate. - BARRIER: Racial inequities in housing and homelessness - Applies to: Black and Latino residents in Greater Boston - Content: Black and Latino residents experience homelessness at far higher rates than White residents. These gaps reflect long‑standing inequities in zoning, investment, and housing access that shape who becomes and remains homeless. - BARRIER: Overwhelmed assistance infrastructure - Applies to: Households seeking help from nonprofits and legal services - Content: Nonprofits and legal aid groups face huge demand with limited staff. Advocates say the old assumption that “there is always somewhere to send people for housing help” no longer reflects reality for many families and individuals. --- ## Additional local context: shelter and housing responses (Boston) - FACT: Shelter utilization and expansion (adult individuals) - Topic: services_shelter_individuals - Content: From 2024–2025, adults in emergency shelters rose 1,544→1,648 as Boston added beds. New programs for men and women aimed to deconcentrate large shelters and spread clients across multiple, less crowded sites.','[0.03179931640625,0.0023822784423828125,-0.005893707275390625,-0.0172119140625,0.06561279296875,0.031768798828125,0.044464111328125,0.0099945068359375,-0.046478271484375,-0.020263671875,-0.040008544921875,-0.038482666015625,-0.055023193359375,0.0245361328125,-0.0005941390991210938,0.039764404296875,0.08697509765625,0.01554107666015625,0.00899505615234375,-0.0272369384765625,0.0479736328125,0.01519775390625,-0.02117919921875,0.00983428955078125,0.03515625,-0.009124755859375,-0.001926422119140625,-0.0272979736328125,-0.052703857421875,-0.02288818359375,0.045074462890625,-0.0440673828125,-0.0190887451171875,-0.051177978515625,0.0248565673828