INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(49,'dc',1,'- Content: From 2023–2024, unaccompanied individuals increased 5.6%, while people in families increased 41.3%. Since 2020, unaccompanied counts are nearly flat, but people in families are down 31.9%. - FACT: Unsheltered vs sheltered - City: Washington, DC - Topic: unsheltered_vs_sheltered - Content: In 2024, 84% of people were in shelter or transitional housing. 900 people were unsheltered, mostly unaccompanied adults, with only 5 unsheltered family households and 1 unaccompanied minor. - FACT: System inflow and churn - City: Washington, DC - Topic: system_inflow - Content: In FY23, about 40% of unaccompanied individuals served (≈3,460 people) and 35% of families were new or had returned after two+ years in housing. New inflow keeps counts from falling. - FACT: Geographic clusters of unsheltered homelessness - City: Washington, DC - Topic: unsheltered_geography - Content: Unsheltered people are concentrated in central areas such as Downtown, Union Station, Georgetown, Foggy Bottom, and the Golden Triangle, where survey teams found large clusters. ### Demographic patterns - FACT: Race and ethnicity - Topic: demographics_race - Content: In 2024, 93% of people counted identified with a race/ethnicity other than White alone, versus 62% in the general DC population. 8% of people in families and 12% of unaccompanied individuals identified as Hispanic/Latinx.','[0.0347900390625,-0.0221710205078125,0.022064208984375,0.00833892822265625,0.06365966796875,0.0074920654296875,0.06414794921875,0.063720703125,-0.056427001953125,-0.0518798828125,-0.0491943359375,-0.0439453125,-0.07562255859375,0.0222015380859375,0.0189971923828125,0.03802490234375,0.071044921875,-0.02081298828125,0.013336181640625,0.00833892822265625,0.0292816162109375,-0.01503753662109375,0.03302001953125,0.0032958984375,0.04119873046875,-0.0258331298828125,0.051239013671875,-0.059814453125,-0.0738525390625,0.00290679931640625,0.015960693359375,-0.0004858970642089844,-0.02