INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(50,'dc',2,'e counted identified with a race/ethnicity other than White alone, versus 62% in the general DC population. 8% of people in families and 12% of unaccompanied individuals identified as Hispanic/Latinx. - FACT: Age groups - Topic: demographics_age - Content: The median age was 45 for unaccompanied individuals (46 men, 45 women) and 30 for heads of family households. Unaccompanied adults have skewed younger since 2022, while adults in families have become slightly older. - FACT: Gender patterns - Topic: demographics_gender - Content: Women are 86% of adults in families, while men are 70% of unaccompanied adults. About 2% of unaccompanied adults (92 people) identify with a gender other than solely man or woman, compared to 6 adults in families. --- ## Contributing factors and life experiences ### Contextual factors - FACT: Pandemic-era supports and readjustment - Topic: contributing_factors_policy_context - Content: Recent increases may reflect a rebound after extra public health emergency resources ended. As those supports expired, more people and families re‑entered homelessness or came into the system. - FACT: System strain from new and returning households - Topic: contributing_factors_inflow - Content: High inflow of people new to the CoC or returning after prior exits to housing undermines progress.','[0.00688934326171875,-0.0222625732421875,0.01541900634765625,0.00373077392578125,0.041534423828125,0.015625,0.060516357421875,0.059326171875,-0.052886962890625,-0.02032470703125,-0.03515625,-0.0295867919921875,-0.0548095703125,0.0024356842041015625,-0.0287322998046875,0.048828125,0.060089111328125,-0.01210784912109375,0.039947509765625,0.01184844970703125,0.023101806640625,-0.03271484375,0.0162200927734375,0.030731201171875,0.043487548828125,-0.0513916015625,0.0092926025390625,-0.04901123046875,-0.06390380859375,-0.00408172607421875,0.0189208984375,-0.0170135498046875,0.001495361328125,-0.016357421875,0.020721435546875,-0.001