INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(52,'dc',4,'he veteran count fell by 5 people in 2024 and by 96 (–45%) since 2020. In FY23, 335 veterans were housed, a 33% increase over FY22, and most veterans served were single adults rather than in families. ### Disabling conditions and chronic homelessness - FACT: Disabling conditions – unaccompanied adults - Topic: conditions_unaccompanied - Content: Unaccompanied adults show high rates of mental illness, substance use history, chronic health issues, disabilities, and HIV. About 43% meet criteria for chronic homelessness, far higher than adults in families. - FACT: Disabling conditions – adults in families - Topic: conditions_families - Content: Adults in families have much lower rates of disabling conditions and chronic homelessness than unaccompanied adults. Faster exits from shelter to housing among families also help keep chronic homelessness low in this group. --- ## Shelter, transitional housing, and unsheltered settings ### Unaccompanied individuals - FACT: Shelter and transitional housing – unaccompanied - Topic: services_shelter_individuals - Content: From 2023–2024, unaccompanied individuals in shelter or transitional housing increased 5.6%. Since 2020, they are down 9.7% in emergency shelters but up 4.1% in transitional housing; 9 unaccompanied minors were in a youth‑specific shelter.','[-0.001399993896484375,0.002819061279296875,0.007472991943359375,-0.016357421875,0.053955078125,-0.010009765625,0.0828857421875,0.048675537109375,-0.05615234375,-0.03570556640625,-0.07391357421875,-0.007289886474609375,-0.04888916015625,0.0595703125,0.019073486328125,0.0560302734375,0.060516357421875,-0.0211334228515625,0.022735595703125,-0.00884246826171875,0.017791748046875,0.0001214146614074707,0.018341064453125,0.01404571533203125,0.039520263671875,-0.029052734375,0.034912109375,-0.0306549072265625,-0.04656982421875,-0.01372528076171875,-0.0006527900695800781,-0.0277099609375,-0.027740478515625,-0.0283660888671875,0.0369873046875,0.