INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(53,'dc',5,'ls in shelter or transitional housing increased 5.6%. Since 2020, they are down 9.7% in emergency shelters but up 4.1% in transitional housing; 9 unaccompanied minors were in a youth‑specific shelter. ### Families - FACT: Shelter and transitional housing – families - Topic: services_shelter_families - Content: From 2023–2024, families in shelter or transitional housing rose 38.6%. Since 2020, families in emergency shelters are down 50.4%, while those in transitional housing are up 32.4%; no pregnant or parenting minors were counted in 2024. ### Unsheltered persons - FACT: Unsheltered persons - Topic: unsheltered_detail - Content: In 2024, 900 people were unsheltered: 887 unaccompanied adults, 1 unaccompanied 17‑year‑old, and 5 families (5 adults, 7 children). Unsheltered unaccompanied person counts are up 8.2% since 2023 and 36% since 2020. --- ## Income and employment - FACT: Income and employment – unaccompanied adults - Topic: income_unaccompanied - Content: Unaccompanied adults report lower employment and income rates than adults in families. Among those with income, most rely on benefits as their primary source, often disability income rather than wages. - FACT: Income and employment – adults in families - Topic: income_families - Content: Adults in families are more likely to have income and employment than unaccompanied adults.','[0.005268096923828125,-0.015045166015625,0.004779815673828125,-0.01873779296875,0.086181640625,-0.0027408599853515625,0.06475830078125,0.060333251953125,-0.040252685546875,-0.050628662109375,-0.058441162109375,-0.04156494140625,-0.03619384765625,0.024383544921875,0.0105133056640625,0.039398193359375,0.08099365234375,-0.01261138916015625,0.02850341796875,0.00244903564453125,0.011260986328125,-0.007061004638671875,0.00864410400390625,-0.006580352783203125,0.0438232421875,-0.032257080078125,0.037689208984375,-0.0308685302734375,-0.0662841796875,0.0123443603515625,0.0124053955078125,-0.0025348663