INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(55,'la',0,'# City: Los Angeles, CA # Scope: Homelessness context and resources # Timeframe: Data primarily from 2023–2024 (LA County and City of LA) ## Summary (High-level) - In 2024, LA County counted ~75,312 people experiencing homelessness; 45,252 were in the City of LA. Countywide totals dipped slightly, and shelter use rose. - Unsheltered homelessness declined while shelter placements and rehousing flow increased, partly due to encampment resolutions and coordinated emergency efforts. - High rents, housing shortages, income inequality, mental illness, substance use, climate, and governance challenges all contribute to LA’s large and visible homeless population. --- ## Overall statistics and trends ### Population level and trends - FACT: Overall homeless population - City: Los Angeles (County and City) - Topic: population_trend - Content: In 2024, LA County’s homeless population was about 75,312, down ~0.27% from 2023. The City of LA’s count was about 45,252, a 2.2% decrease from the prior year.','[0.034515380859375,-0.046142578125,0.040130615234375,-0.00547027587890625,0.0770263671875,0.0380859375,0.05877685546875,0.051849365234375,-0.03515625,-0.03271484375,-0.053619384765625,-0.0323486328125,-0.0731201171875,0.016571044921875,-0.0119476318359375,0.065673828125,0.09161376953125,-0.0021724700927734375,0.04388427734375,-0.01007843017578125,0.028228759765625,0.001506805419921875,-0.0198211669921875,0.042938232421875,0.0335693359375,-0.002407073974609375,0.019134521484375,-0.00676727294921875,-0.08782958984375,0.00048232078552246094,0.0196685791015625,-0.00494384765625,-0.0266265869140625,-0.04595947265625,0.016510009765625,-0.01219940185546875,0.0034313201904296875,-0.032196044921875,0.00023484230041503906,0.0286712646484375,-0.017333984375,-0.032745361328125,-0.01044464111328125,0.001544952392578125,-0.0509033203125,-0.0189208984375,0.019378662109375,0.0012731552124023438,0.0238189697265625,0.0246734619140625,-0.055419921875,0.0068