INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(56,'la',1,'ty) - Topic: population_trend - Content: In 2024, LA County’s homeless population was about 75,312, down ~0.27% from 2023. The City of LA’s count was about 45,252, a 2.2% decrease from the prior year. - FACT: Unsheltered vs sheltered – County - City: Los Angeles County - Topic: unsheltered_vs_sheltered - Content: Countywide in 2024, about 52,365 people were unsheltered and 22,847 were sheltered. Compared with 2023, unsheltered homelessness fell 5.1% while sheltered homelessness rose 12.7%. - FACT: Unsheltered vs sheltered – City of LA - City: Los Angeles (City) - Topic: unsheltered_vs_sheltered_city - Content: In the City of LA, unsheltered homelessness dropped by about 10.4% from 2023 to 2024. Over the same period, the number of people in shelter increased by roughly 17.7%. - FACT: Dwelling types (vehicles, tents, makeshift) - City: Los Angeles - Topic: unsheltered_dwellings - Content: Between 2023 and 2024, counts in cars, vans, and tents fell modestly, RVs stayed nearly flat, and makeshift shelters dropped by about 30%. Overall, these dwelling types decreased roughly 9%. - FACT: System performance – rehousing flow - City: Los Angeles County - Topic: housing_system_performance - Content: In 2023, LA’s rehousing system logged a record number of permanent housing placements.','[0.043060302734375,-0.040374755859375,0.050262451171875,0.0018892288208007812,0.06988525390625,0.0194549560546875,0.0477294921875,0.043060302734375,-0.025390625,-0.0297088623046875,-0.045654296875,-0.01171112060546875,-0.07861328125,0.02130126953125,-0.0038356781005859375,0.08355712890625,0.0960693359375,-0.01506805419921875,0.0166473388671875,-0.01181793212890625,0.035736083984375,-0.00992584228515625,-0.0202178955078125,0.0196075439453125,0.037933349609375,0.003223419189453125,0.043792724609375,-0.014892578125,-0.0821533203125,-0.0025310516357421875,0.0242462158203125,0.0168914794921875,-0.022674560546875,-0.0104522705078125,0.00698089599609375,-0.02