INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(57,'la',2,'CT: System performance – rehousing flow - City: Los Angeles County - Topic: housing_system_performance - Content: In 2023, LA’s rehousing system logged a record number of permanent housing placements. From 2022–2023, street‑to‑interim placements via outreach rose nearly 50%, and interim‑to‑permanent moves rose about 25%. - FACT: Chronic homelessness trend - City: Los Angeles CoC - Topic: population_trend_chronic - Content: The CoC reports a drop in chronic homelessness, suggesting the coordinated emergency response and rehousing strategies are helping people with long‑term homelessness exit streets and encampments. ### Demographic patterns - FACT: Age groups - Topic: demographics_age - Content: From 2023–2024, adults 18–54 experiencing homelessness decreased by about 2.7%, while older adults 55+ increased 6.5%. The number of children (0–17) changed little. - FACT: Race and ethnicity (overall) - Topic: demographics_race - Content: Black residents remain disproportionately represented, reflecting historic exclusionary policies. Latinos are the largest ethnic group experiencing homelessness, making up about 43% when including mixed categories.','[0.0243072509765625,-0.031890869140625,0.059051513671875,-0.00838470458984375,0.07000732421875,0.04449462890625,0.04156494140625,0.049163818359375,-0.01861572265625,-0.061614990234375,-0.039825439453125,-0.047027587890625,-0.071044921875,0.00885772705078125,0.00849151611328125,0.05126953125,0.070556640625,-0.006805419921875,0.0350341796875,-0.033660888671875,0.019866943359375,-0.000003159046173095703,-0.014434814453125,0.0404052734375,0.01953125,-0.0081787109375,0.01123809814453125,-0.033966064453125,-0.06695556640625,-0.01103973388671875,0.04693603515625,-0.012481689453125,-0.0240020751953125,-0.02447509765625,0.0209197998046875,0.00853729248046875,-0.004669189453125,-0.023040771484375,-0.003940582275390625,-0.0007543563842773438,-0.030242919921875,-0.016845703125,-0.039581298828125,-0