INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(58,'la',3,'s remain disproportionately represented, reflecting historic exclusionary policies. Latinos are the largest ethnic group experiencing homelessness, making up about 43% when including mixed categories. - FACT: Race and ethnicity (detailed) - Topic: demographics_race_detail - Content: In 2024, about 31% of people experiencing homelessness identified as Black, around 29% as White, several percent as Indigenous, Asian, Pacific Islander, or multiracial, and more than 40% identified as Hispanic/Latino/a/e alone or with another race. - FACT: Gender diversity - Topic: demographics_gender - Content: Men and boys were the largest group, with more than 46,000 people. Women and girls accounted for about 23,000, and smaller numbers identified as transgender, non‑binary, culturally specific identities, or more than one gender. ### Health and behavioral health - FACT: Serious mental illness (SMI) - Topic: conditions_smi - Content: In 2024, about 24% of unhoused people in the LA CoC reported serious mental illness, slightly down from 25% in 2023. Unsheltered SMI counts declined, while more people with SMI were in shelter. - FACT: Substance use disorder (SUD) - Topic: conditions_sud - Content: About 27% reported substance use disorder in 2024, down from 30% in 2023. Unsheltered SUD counts dropped notably, while sheltered SUD counts increased, indicating more engagement indoors.','[0.0120697021484375,-0.00861358642578125,0.005527496337890625,-0.0130615234375,0.057647705078125,0.0394287109375,0.04583740234375,0.03326416015625,-0.049896240234375,-0.0027313232421875,-0.036407470703125,-0.0270233154296875,-0.06805419921875,0.0176544189453125,-0.0038394927978515625,0.0546875,0.0758056640625,-0.004779815673828125,0.0240020751953125,0.004863739013671875,0.046600341796875,-0.012481689453125,-0.00853729248046875,0.0263824462890625,0.03497314453125,-0.005474090576171875,0.00946044921875,-0.0511474609375,-0.061920166015625,-0.01120758056640625,0.0309295