INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(59,'la',4,'d - Content: About 27% reported substance use disorder in 2024, down from 30% in 2023. Unsheltered SUD counts dropped notably, while sheltered SUD counts increased, indicating more engagement indoors. --- ## Contributing factors and reasons for homelessness - FACT: Economic hardship and first-time homelessness - Topic: contributing_factors_economic - Content: Among newly homeless unsheltered people, 54% cited economic hardship as a reason. Others mentioned weakened social networks, disabling health conditions, system discharge, violence, or other causes, often in combination. - FACT: Housing costs and wages - Topic: contributing_factors_housing_costs - Content: Unaffordable rent is a central driver. The average two‑bedroom rent in LA County is about $2,498, requiring roughly $48 an hour to afford, which many renters do not earn. - FACT: Housing supply and permits - Topic: contributing_factors_housing_supply - Content: Nearly 495,000 California households lack access to an affordable home. Building permits fell 7% in 2023, and early 2024 multifamily permits were a third lower than the same period in 2023. - FACT: Evictions and rental debt - Topic: contributing_factors_evictions - Content: From February to December 2023, about 77,000 eviction notices were filed in the City of LA.','[0.033203125,0.003887176513671875,0.023284912109375,-0.00409698486328125,0.06640625,0.0212249755859375,0.062042236328125,0.03936767578125,-0.0274200439453125,-0.04461669921875,-0.047882080078125,-0.0269927978515625,-0.0623779296875,0.019622802734375,0.0279541015625,0.0616455078125,0.076904296875,-0.030059814453125,0.0030956268310546875,-0.0174407958984375,0.046600341796875,0.0098724365234375,-0.002048492431640625,0.0234222412109375,0.042327880859375,-0.016265869140625,-0.0055389404296875,-0.0262451171875,-0.0782470703125,-0.011077880859375,0.0194549560546875,0.0251922607421875,0.002361297607421875,-0.03887939453125,0.039276123046875,0.0255126953125,