INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(60,'la',5,'he same period in 2023. - FACT: Evictions and rental debt - Topic: contributing_factors_evictions - Content: From February to December 2023, about 77,000 eviction notices were filed in the City of LA. Around 96% were for non‑payment of rent, most with three‑day notices, and average rent owed was about $3,774. - FACT: Role of population size and density - Topic: contributing_factors_population - Content: LA County has about 10 million residents across 88 cities and a large urban core. High population and density increase housing pressure and make homelessness more visible in central neighborhoods. - FACT: Climate and geography - Topic: contributing_factors_climate - Content: LA’s mild climate and outdoor spaces (such as beaches and parks) make unsheltered survival more feasible. This can draw people from other regions and contributes to large, visible encampments. - FACT: Mental health, SUD, and service gaps - Topic: contributing_factors_behavioral_health - Content: Many unhoused people live with serious mental illness or substance use disorders. Limited, hard‑to‑access treatment and ongoing service gaps worsen conditions and complicate long‑term stability. - FACT: Income inequality - Topic: contributing_factors_income_inequality - Content: LA has a wide gap between high‑income and low‑income residents.','[0.0263214111328125,-0.03436279296875,0.042938232421875,0.01239013671875,0.04656982421875,0.00824737548828125,0.060882568359375,0.037139892578125,-0.04022216796875,-0.03265380859375,-0.05548095703125,-0.006649017333984375,-0.05633544921875,0.0242767333984375,0.007904052734375,0.06512451171875,0.05194091796875,-0.01299285888671875,0.022613525390625,-0.0148162841796875,0.01409912109375,0.021484375,-0.01336669921875,0.034027099609375,0.045806884765625,-0.007549285888671875,0.007518768310546875,-0.006793975830078125,-0.08929443359375,-0.00017714500427246094,-0.0032672882080078125,0.0245208740234375,-0.01360321044921875,-0.006900