INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(61,'la',6,'rsen conditions and complicate long‑term stability. - FACT: Income inequality - Topic: contributing_factors_income_inequality - Content: LA has a wide gap between high‑income and low‑income residents. This inequality leaves many households on the edge of housing insecurity, especially when rents rise and wages do not keep pace. - FACT: Service capacity limits - Topic: contributing_factors_service_capacity - Content: Despite major investments, shelters and supportive programs often cannot meet demand. System capacity, staffing, and funding constraints mean many people still do not get the help they need when they need it. - FACT: Governance and legal context - Topic: contributing_factors_governance - Content: LA County’s fragmented political structure complicates collective action. Legal debates, including around ordinances like 41.18, shape how encampments and public space are managed and affect service delivery. - FACT: Short-term vs comprehensive solutions - Topic: contributing_factors_solutions - Content: Short‑term responses alone have not fully addressed root causes such as housing costs, income inequality, and behavioral health gaps. Sustained, comprehensive strategies are needed to change long‑term trends.','[0.040008544921875,-0.056854248046875,-0.004940032958984375,0.0204620361328125,0.0654296875,0.0304718017578125,0.05364990234375,0.005939483642578125,-0.048583984375,-0.025146484375,-0.00102996826171875,-0.015716552734375,-0.06512451171875,0.040252685546875,-0.016082763671875,0.07293701171875,0.06927490234375,0.0019817352294921875,0.004039764404296875,0.0135955810546875,0.01209259033203125,0.0299530029296875,0.018951416015625,0.020782470703125,0.0307464599609375,0.0037097930908203125,-0.01605224609375,-0.0241851806640625,-0.043121337890625,-0.0086822509765625,0.0396728515625,0.0000756978988647461,-0.02337646484375,-0.0157623291015625,0.0075531005859375,-0.0150299072265625,-0.048004150390625,0.0033779144287109375,-0