INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(67,'nyc',2,'350,000+. - FACT: Children and families (statewide) - City: New York (Statewide) - Topic: population_children_state - Content: Homeless children increased from about 20,299 in 2022 to 50,773 in 2024. Nearly one in three people experiencing homelessness statewide is a child, one of the highest child shares in the U.S. - FACT: Children and families (NYC schools) - City: New York City - Topic: population_children_nyc_schools - Content: In the 2024–2025 school year, more than 156,000 NYC students experienced homelessness at some point, about one in eight city schoolchildren. - FACT: NYC shelter composition (families vs singles) - City: New York City - Topic: population_families_vs_singles - Content: In November 2025, about 68% of shelter residents were members of homeless families, including 34,393 children. Around 32,668 single adults slept in shelters, and about 31,629 shelter residents were classified as New Arrivals. - FACT: Pandemic era trends - City: New York (Statewide) - Topic: population_trend_pandemic - Content: Homelessness declined in New York between 2020 and 2022 amid pandemic protections. After eviction moratoriums ended, it rose rapidly, more than doubling by 2024 while the rest of the U.S. increased much more slowly.','[-0.0137481689453125,-0.0667724609375,0.023895263671875,-0.0014743804931640625,0.07000732421875,0.0230712890625,0.057891845703125,0.061767578125,-0.0208587646484375,-0.0247955322265625,-0.045562744140625,-0.0374755859375,-0.07965087890625,0.042236328125,-0.0220184326171875,0.032745361328125,0.059600830078125,0.01861572265625,-0.0005431175231933594,-0.0174560546875,-0.01250457763671875,-0.022796630859375,0.0179901123046875,0.014862060546875,0.00405120849609375,-0.00865936279296875,0.006465911865234375,-0.040252685546875,-0.05120849609375,-0.024810791015625,0.0010328292846679688,0.0115966796875,0.00392913818359375,0.0162811279296875,0.0154266357421875,-0.00878143310546875,-0.01090240478515625,0.002