INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(68,'nyc',3,'clined in New York between 2020 and 2022 amid pandemic protections. After eviction moratoriums ended, it rose rapidly, more than doubling by 2024 while the rest of the U.S. increased much more slowly. --- ## Demographic patterns - FACT: Race and ethnicity – statewide - Topic: demographics_race_state - Content: Statewide, Black and Latino/a/e/x New Yorkers are overrepresented among people experiencing homelessness. White residents are the majority of the population but under half of the unhoused, while Black residents are a much larger share of the unhoused. - FACT: Race and ethnicity – detailed statewide - Topic: demographics_race_state_detail - Content: White people are about 68.5% of New York’s population but around 46% of the unhoused. Black residents are about 15.9% of the population yet roughly 51% of the unhoused, showing stark racial inequity. - FACT: Race and ethnicity – NYC shelters - Topic: demographics_race_nyc - Content: Among heads of household in NYC shelters, about 56% are Black, 32% Hispanic/Latinx, 7% White, and less than 1% Asian-American or Native American. A small share is reported as unknown race/ethnicity. - FACT: Age groups – statewide - Topic: demographics_age_state - Content: More than 50,000 people experiencing homelessness in New York are children, and over 14,000 are seniors.','[0.011322021484375,-0.059661865234375,0.01122283935546875,-0.0278472900390625,0.06976318359375,-0.003162384033203125,0.06036376953125,0.0443115234375,-0.02716064453125,-0.02349853515625,-0.013946533203125,-0.049407958984375,-0.0694580078125,0.005519866943359375,-0.00391387939453125,0.0565185546875,0.06341552734375,-0.019775390625,0.0024814605712890625,-0.0192108154296875,0.00992584228515625,-0.0182037353515625,0.0134429931640625,0.0239410400390625,0.0233917236328125,-0.0242462158203125,0.010894775390625,-0.0660400390625,-0.06414794921875,-0.01479339599609375,-0.0017547607421875,-0.002498626708984375,-0.02435302734375,-0.01