INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(69,'nyc',4,'known race/ethnicity. - FACT: Age groups – statewide - Topic: demographics_age_state - Content: More than 50,000 people experiencing homelessness in New York are children, and over 14,000 are seniors. The state overall has relatively low shares of senior homelessness compared to some states but large absolute numbers. --- ## Subpopulations and conditions - FACT: Veterans (statewide) - Topic: subpopulation_veterans_state - Content: Statewide veteran homelessness remains low, below 1% of all people experiencing homelessness. It rose only about 1%, with stability linked to targeted rental assistance and outreach such as HUD‑VASH. - FACT: Veterans (NYC) - Topic: subpopulation_veterans_nyc - Content: New York is among the states with low shares of veterans in the homeless population. This is seen as a success of sustained federal and local investments focused specifically on veterans. - FACT: Seniors and chronic homelessness (statewide) - Topic: subpopulation_seniors_chronic - Content: New York has relatively low shares of seniors (about 2.5%) and chronically homeless people (about 3.6%) compared with many states. However, the absolute numbers remain significant in a large population. - FACT: Asylum seekers and New Arrivals (NYC) - Topic: subpopulation_asylum_seekers - Content: Tens of thousands of asylum seekers arrived in NYC, many with no housing options.','[0.003719329833984375,-0.03399658203125,0.0307769775390625,0.0268096923828125,0.06964111328125,0.0452880859375,0.045257568359375,0.03790283203125,-0.02374267578125,-0.022796630859375,-0.047271728515625,-0.005413055419921875,-0.059112548828125,0.0301666259765625,-0.0192413330078125,0.06268310546875,0.06463623046875,-0.010894775390625,0.0204925537109375,-0.01177978515625,-0.01165008544921875,-0.0005621910095214844,0.024810791015625,0.02801513671875,0.0191497802734375,-0.004726409912109375,0.02459716796875,-0.048248291015625,-0.048858642578125,-0.0183868408203125,0.0004775524