INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(70,'nyc',5,'in a large population. - FACT: Asylum seekers and New Arrivals (NYC) - Topic: subpopulation_asylum_seekers - Content: Tens of thousands of asylum seekers arrived in NYC, many with no housing options. By January 2024, about 34,000 asylum seekers were in DHS shelters and around 68,000 were housed by the city overall. - FACT: Disabilities and health (NYC longer-term residents) - Topic: conditions_disability_nyc - Content: Among longer-term NYC shelter residents (non-New Arrivals), 43% of families with children, 65% of single adults, and 75% of adult-only families have a disability that needs a facility-related accommodation. - FACT: Health and behavioral health (statewide) - Topic: conditions_statewide - Content: About 10% of people experiencing homelessness statewide have severe mental illness or chronic substance use disorders. These conditions compound barriers to housing and stability. - FACT: Unsheltered population characteristics (NYC) - Topic: conditions_unsheltered_nyc - Content: Most unsheltered individuals in NYC are people living with mental illness or other severe health problems. Reliable counts of unsheltered people are difficult, and official estimates may be low.','[-0.0243988037109375,-0.01381683349609375,0.00263214111328125,0.0184478759765625,0.06256103515625,0.018218994140625,0.05023193359375,0.04400634765625,-0.042205810546875,-0.013458251953125,-0.058563232421875,-0.041015625,-0.076416015625,0.0289306640625,0.024200439453125,0.03692626953125,0.07489013671875,-0.0023193359375,0.002574920654296875,-0.00547027587890625,0.01079559326171875,-0.019378662109375,0.023101806640625,0.01015472412109375,0.039794921875,-0.039215087890625,0.02813720703125,-0.043365478515625,-0.042083740234375,0.01116943359375,-0.0016183853149414062,-0.02301025390625,-0.0477294921875,-0.02044677734375,-0.005962371826171875,0.0013074874877929688,-0.05816650390625,0.018524169921875,-0.00881195068359375,-0.02099609375,-0.026092529296875,0.0