INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(71,'nyc',6,'tent: Most unsheltered individuals in NYC are people living with mental illness or other severe health problems. Reliable counts of unsheltered people are difficult, and official estimates may be low. --- ## Unsheltered vs sheltered and system capacity - FACT: Unsheltered share – statewide - City: New York (Statewide) - Topic: unsheltered_vs_sheltered - Content: New York has the lowest share of unsheltered people in the U.S., at about 3.6%, compared with roughly 44% in the rest of the country. This reflects robust shelter mandates and infrastructure. - FACT: Emergency shelter capacity - City: New York (Statewide) - Topic: services_shelter_capacity - Content: New York has about 127,759 year‑round emergency housing beds, including roughly 122,091 in emergency shelters. This is far more than any other state and is largely due to NYC’s right‑to‑shelter obligations. - FACT: Supportive and permanent housing capacity - City: New York (Statewide) - Topic: services_psh_capacity - Content: New York has about 52,462 permanent supportive housing units, second only to California. It also has over 21,600 permanent housing beds, but far fewer rapid rehousing beds than some other large states.','[0.0302734375,-0.051300048828125,-0.0265350341796875,-0.007762908935546875,0.0771484375,0.01202392578125,0.036712646484375,0.054901123046875,-0.01287841796875,-0.0325927734375,0.005035400390625,-0.046478271484375,-0.0855712890625,0.040191650390625,0.0053253173828125,0.044036865234375,0.08154296875,0.010589599609375,-0.0264129638671875,0.0253753662109375,0.0731201171875,-0.00887298583984375,0.00992584228515625,-0.01084136962890625,0.0204010009765625,-0.022003173828125,0.05218505859375,-0.0477294921875,-0.05279541015625,0.00231170654296875,0.0213470458984375,0.0048828125,-0.018218994140625,-0.0183868408203125,0.038604736328125,-0.01611328125,-0.069091796875,0.016937255859375,-0.028350830078125,0.005855560302734375,-0.0169677734375,-0.035247802734375,