INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(72,'nyc',7,'ew York has about 52,462 permanent supportive housing units, second only to California. It also has over 21,600 permanent housing beds, but far fewer rapid rehousing beds than some other large states. --- ## Contributing factors and reasons for homelessness - FACT: Housing affordability crisis (statewide) - Topic: contributing_factors_housing_costs - Content: Long‑standing housing affordability problems, rising rents, and a shortage of affordable units push many households into homelessness. HUD cites evictions, rent increases, and limited affordable housing as key drivers. - FACT: Asylum seekers and cost pressures - Topic: contributing_factors_asylum_seekers - Content: Tens of thousands of asylum seekers arriving with no housing options drove much of the recent surge, especially in NYC. Their sheltering needs sharply increased public spending and system demand. - FACT: Evictions and post‑moratorium impact - Topic: contributing_factors_evictions - Content: After pandemic eviction moratoriums ended, eviction filings and proceedings resumed. This change coincided with a sharp rise in homelessness between 2022 and 2024 as more families lost housing. - FACT: Employment and wages - Topic: contributing_factors_employment - Content: About half of people experiencing homelessness statewide are employed, yet still cannot afford housing.','[0.0161285400390625,-0.04608154296875,0.0396728515625,-0.0082855224609375,0.06268310546875,0.032989501953125,0.0582275390625,0.031494140625,-0.0159454345703125,-0.047119140625,-0.03448486328125,-0.05029296875,-0.0533447265625,0.037811279296875,0.025482177734375,0.0295867919921875,0.03326416015625,-0.01031494140625,-0.0179443359375,-0.040130615234375,0.04559326171875,0.00921630859375,0.030029296875,0.026214599609375,0.0016469955444335938,-0.03643798828125,0.003322601318359375,-0.07061767578125,-0.052886962890625,-0.0191802978515625,0.005428314208984375,0.00670623779296875,-0.01334381103515625,-0.000