INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(73,'nyc',8,'s lost housing. - FACT: Employment and wages - Topic: contributing_factors_employment - Content: About half of people experiencing homelessness statewide are employed, yet still cannot afford housing. Rents outpacing wages mean work alone is no longer a guarantee against homelessness. - FACT: Racialized inequities - Topic: contributing_factors_racial_inequity - Content: Black and Latino/a/e/x New Yorkers are far more likely to experience homelessness than their share of the population suggests. These disparities reflect long‑standing inequities in housing, wages, and systems. - FACT: Causes of homelessness – NYC families - Topic: contributing_factors_families_nyc - Content: Surveys of homeless families in NYC cite eviction, severe overcrowding or doubling up, domestic violence, job loss, and unsafe housing as the main immediate triggers for entering shelter. - FACT: Mental health, substances, and fentanyl - Topic: contributing_factors_behavioral_health - Content: Rising mental health challenges, substance use, and the spread of fentanyl in street drugs are noted as contributing to homelessness and making recovery and stability more difficult.','[0.0382080078125,-0.01422119140625,-0.0025653839111328125,0.01180267333984375,0.061065673828125,0.05755615234375,0.0537109375,0.036834716796875,-0.01122283935546875,-0.059051513671875,-0.03399658203125,-0.016021728515625,-0.0654296875,0.0146026611328125,-0.0082550048828125,0.03924560546875,0.06707763671875,-0.0083160400390625,0.007537841796875,-0.0114898681640625,0.0177459716796875,0.0132293701171875,0.00548553466796875,0.0229949951171875,0.0108795166015625,-0.041412353515625,-0.0029449462890625,-0.0277862548828125,-0.0679931640625,0.004589080810546875,0.0241851806640625,0.01018524169921875,0.00006133317947387695,-0.039947509765625,0.00489044189453125,0.024139404296875,-0.022247314453125,0.00621795654296875,0.00019752979278564453,0.01947021484375,-0.037139892578125,-0.010643005371093