INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(74,'nyc',9,'health - Content: Rising mental health challenges, substance use, and the spread of fentanyl in street drugs are noted as contributing to homelessness and making recovery and stability more difficult. --- ## NYC policy frameworks and strategies ### Prevention (keep people housed) - FACT: Prevention focus - City: New York City - Topic: prevention_overview - Content: NYC and New York State prioritize prevention to keep people out of shelters. Strategies include supplementing shelter allowances, expanding rental vouchers, and strengthening services for at‑risk households. - FACT: Targeted prevention steps - City: New York City - Topic: prevention_measures - Content: Key steps include better discharge planning from prisons, expanded housing options for people involved in the justice system, support for at‑risk seniors, and improved outreach and enforcement related to unsafe housing. ### Increasing pathways to permanent, affordable housing - FACT: Rental assistance and housing supply - City: New York City - Topic: housing_pathways_vouchers - Content: NYC seeks to raise voucher amounts to fair market rent, expand voucher eligibility, and increase access to deeply affordable housing. Combating source‑of‑income discrimination and engaging landlords are key tactics.','[0.0205230712890625,-0.046844482421875,-0.007556915283203125,0.0138092041015625,0.071533203125,0.034149169921875,0.053497314453125,0.004474639892578125,-0.01381683349609375,-0.0670166015625,-0.0239410400390625,0.0004711151123046875,-0.06890869140625,0.01003265380859375,0.02154541015625,0.036102294921875,0.0909423828125,0.004405975341796875,0.006412506103515625,0.0008740425109863281,0.0288543701171875,0.0284423828125,0.016845703125,0.047515869140625,-0.00010371208190917969,-0.0251617431640625,0.0112457275390625,-0.0177764892578125,-0.0712890625,0.024322509765625,0.03802490234375,-0.003231048583984375,-0.004749298095703125,-0.035186767578125,0.032745361328125,0.024932861