INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(75,'nyc',10,'ise voucher amounts to fair market rent, expand voucher eligibility, and increase access to deeply affordable housing. Combating source‑of‑income discrimination and engaging landlords are key tactics. - FACT: Supportive housing expansion - City: New York (State and City) - Topic: housing_pathways_supportive - Content: The state is implementing a five‑year, $25 billion plan to create or preserve 100,000 affordable homes, including supportive housing. NYC also aims to aggressively build and maintain supportive housing stock. - FACT: Youth and aftercare supports - City: New York City - Topic: housing_pathways_youth_aftercare - Content: Plans call for more housing options for homeless youth, more housing specialists, and stronger aftercare services. The goal is to ensure people remain housed after leaving shelters. ### Support for unsheltered neighbors - FACT: Alternatives to traditional shelters - City: New York City - Topic: services_unsheltered_alternatives - Content: NYC plans to expand Safe Havens and other low‑barrier alternatives to shelters. These options, combined with outreach, are meant to better meet the needs of people living on streets or in hospitals.','[0.02960205078125,-0.0692138671875,0.019134521484375,-0.002490997314453125,0.04461669921875,0.0026988983154296875,0.04296875,0.0328369140625,-0.025238037109375,-0.055084228515625,-0.040618896484375,-0.0094146728515625,-0.05322265625,0.0169830322265625,-0.0040130615234375,0.044342041015625,0.0718994140625,-0.010650634765625,-0.006237030029296875,0.0249176025390625,0.00811767578125,0.035125732421875,0.0296630859375,0.028472900390625,0.00360107421875,-0.011566162109375,0.033660888671875,-0.02374267578125,-0.06878662109375,-0.005764007568359375,0.01149749755859375,0.017181396484375,-0.0223846435546875,-0.0194854736328125,-0.0014781951904296875,0.0175018310546875,-0.0249481201171875,0.0157623291015625,-0.003711700439453125,-0.0192108154296875,-0.0266571044921875,-0.00