INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(76,'nyc',11,': NYC plans to expand Safe Havens and other low‑barrier alternatives to shelters. These options, combined with outreach, are meant to better meet the needs of people living on streets or in hospitals. - FACT: Outreach and medical respite - City: New York City - Topic: services_unsheltered_outreach_respite - Content: Proposals include equipping outreach teams with more tools, using an “all hands‑on deck” approach, and creating robust medical respite programs. These efforts aim to move people from streets to stable housing. ### Support for sheltered neighbors - FACT: Enhancing shelter supports - City: New York City - Topic: services_sheltered_supports - Content: NYC aims to improve services within shelters, including more support for domestic violence survivors, economic empowerment, help for formerly incarcerated people, and stronger supports for runaway and homeless youth. ### Integrating housing and homelessness policy - FACT: Inter-agency coordination - City: New York City - Topic: policy_integration - Content: City leaders emphasize better coordination across agencies so housing and homelessness policy are aligned. The goal is a comprehensive response that prioritizes permanent, affordable housing.','[0.002490997314453125,-0.04840087890625,0.0217742919921875,-0.00904083251953125,0.057586669921875,0.002315521240234375,0.049163818359375,-0.01366424560546875,-0.03460693359375,-0.056396484375,-0.0181884765625,-0.0100250244140625,-0.07806396484375,0.0103912353515625,0.023834228515625,0.03497314453125,0.0902099609375,0.0134735107421875,-0.0276947021484375,0.039306640625,0.00788116455078125,0.0340576171875,0.0274658203125,0.0211639404296875,0.0089569091796875,0.020263671875,0.039642333984375,-0.03973388671875,-0.064453125,-0.029144287109375,0.0313720703125,0.0193634033203125,-0.01442718505859375,-0.031341552734375,0.0116424560546875,-0.004550933837890625,-0.044586181640625,-0.005916595458984375,-0.002758026123046875,-0.0084075