INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(77,'nyc',12,'Content: City leaders emphasize better coordination across agencies so housing and homelessness policy are aligned. The goal is a comprehensive response that prioritizes permanent, affordable housing. ### Long-term vision - FACT: Long-term housing vision - City: New York City - Topic: policy_long_term - Content: Over time, NYC seeks to shift funding toward permanent, affordable housing as the shelter census falls. A long‑term vision would match resources to actual needs and use better data to evaluate outcomes. - FACT: Monitoring and accountability (statewide) - City: New York (Statewide) - Topic: policy_monitoring - Content: State leaders are urged to track goals, spending, and results for current housing plans more closely. Recommendations include expanding rental assistance, eviction defense, and housing aid for families with children. --- ## Rights and legal framework - FACT: Right to shelter (NYC) - City: New York City - Topic: legal_right_to_shelter - Content: NYC’s legal right‑to‑shelter framework, in place since 1981, has provided a way off the streets for more than one million people. It underpins the city’s large shelter system and low unsheltered rates.','[0.004367828369140625,-0.046234130859375,0.00794219970703125,-0.00032782554626464844,0.0670166015625,0.051300048828125,0.016387939453125,0.023773193359375,-0.024322509765625,-0.054718017578125,-0.0308990478515625,-0.0282745361328125,-0.08819580078125,0.030181884765625,-0.001987457275390625,0.038543701171875,0.082275390625,0.00580596923828125,-0.010223388671875,0.00492095947265625,0.01219940185546875,0.0565185546875,0.0278778076171875,0.03466796875,0.021881103515625,-0.0162506103515625,0.03216552734375,-0.03369140625,-0.05511474609375,-0.004657745361328125,0.0188446044921875,-0.03118896484375,-0.0164794921875,-0.0227203369140625,0.0194244384765625,-0.00785064697265625,-0.0195159912109375,0.00493621826171875,-0.003330230712890625,0.0033588409423828125,-0.03494262