INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(79,'portland',1,'r housing - Content: City and county tax dollars support thousands of people who were previously homeless or at high risk of homelessness, including through subsidized housing and prevention programs. ## OVERALL STATISTICS AND CHANGES IN POPULATION (Portland / Multnomah County) ### PATTERN: Homeless population size and growth - City: Portland (Multnomah County) - Topic: population_trend - Content: In early 2024, the county estimated its homeless population at around 11,400 people. By early 2025, that estimate had increased substantially, indicating a sharp year‑over‑year rise in homelessness. ### PATTERN: Shelter capacity and utilization - City: Portland (Multnomah County) - Topic: shelter_capacity - Content: Multnomah County has more shelter beds than ever before, but they are still nearly full most nights, with the large majority of approximately 2,500 beds occupied on a typical night. ### PATTERN: Flow into and out of homelessness - City: Portland (Multnomah County) - Topic: inflow_vs_outflow - Content: People are entering homelessness in Multnomah County at a higher rate than they are exiting. Many more people are newly identified as homeless than are recorded as moving into stable housing in a given year.','[0.002475738525390625,-0.037567138671875,0.022735595703125,0.00384521484375,0.08740234375,0.04095458984375,0.0457763671875,0.038818359375,-0.035400390625,-0.052703857421875,-0.0281219482421875,-0.035125732421875,-0.09588623046875,0.0176544189453125,-0.00006628036499023438,0.0531005859375,0.083740234375,-0.0181121826171875,0.0291595458984375,0.0012969970703125,0.0201568603515625,-0.013153076171875,-0.0062713623046875,0.026580810546875,0.049041748046875,-0.0228271484375,0.0253143310546875,-0.012054443359375,-0.07940673828125,0.00548553466796875,0.02880859375,-0.004085540771484375,-0.01470947265625,-0.02105712890625,0.030242919921875,-0.00838470458984375,-0.0006351470947265625,-0.01264190673828125,-0.0080795288085