INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(80,'portland',2,'are entering homelessness in Multnomah County at a higher rate than they are exiting. Many more people are newly identified as homeless than are recorded as moving into stable housing in a given year. ### PATTERN: Publicly funded housing and prevention - City: Portland (Multnomah County) - Topic: housing_subsidies - Content: City and county tax dollars support housing for thousands of people who were previously homeless or at risk of homelessness, and many more receive rent subsidies or permanent housing assistance. This funding helps prevent homelessness but does not fully offset the broader housing shortage. ### PATTERN: Affordable housing waitlists and income levels - City: Portland (Multnomah County) - Topic: affordable_housing_waitlist - Content: Waitlists for public and subsidized housing in Portland are long, with many applicants categorized as extremely low income. A substantial portion of those on waitlists either are currently homeless or have very unstable housing, meaning long waits can keep people in precarious or street situations for years. ### PATTERN: Vehicle-based homelessness - City: Portland (Multnomah County) - Topic: vehicle_homelessness - Content: A notable portion of unsheltered people in the county live in vehicles such as cars, vans, or RVs.','[0.00885772705078125,-0.025299072265625,0.004917144775390625,0.039306640625,0.0760498046875,0.0509033203125,0.050262451171875,0.031524658203125,-0.0313720703125,-0.0677490234375,-0.01067352294921875,-0.0203399658203125,-0.08001708984375,0.0137481689453125,-0.00868988037109375,0.05694580078125,0.075927734375,-0.000885009765625,0.0014772415161132812,-0.014495849609375,0.033966064453125,0.00684356689453125,-0.0007205009460449219,0.03875732421875,0.046417236328125,-0.007312774658203125,0.01910400390625,0.01200103759765625,-0.09063720703125,-0.0013885498046875,0.032501220703125,0.0135345458984375,-0.00013756752014160156,-0.033355712890625,0.0269012451171875,-