INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(81,'portland',3,'hicle-based homelessness - City: Portland (Multnomah County) - Topic: vehicle_homelessness - Content: A notable portion of unsheltered people in the county live in vehicles such as cars, vans, or RVs. Many of them were priced out of rental housing or evicted and turned to living in vehicles as a last step before unsheltered tent camping. ## CONTRIBUTING FACTORS TO HOMELESSNESS IN PORTLAND ### FACTOR: Affordable housing shortage - Type: structural_factor - Content: Portland has a major shortage of affordable housing. Demand is high while the supply of low‑cost units is limited, and long waitlists for subsidized units keep many people in unstable or homeless situations. ### FACTOR: Rising rents and cost of living - Type: structural_factor - Content: Rents and basic living costs have been increasing faster than many residents’ incomes, leading to rent burden, evictions, and people being priced out of their homes. ### FACTOR: Evictions and housing instability - Type: pathway_to_homelessness - Content: Many people enter homelessness after a period of housing instability that includes late rent payments, informal arrangements such as couch‑surfing, and eventual eviction. Losing a rental makes it much harder to secure another unit, especially with poor credit or an eviction record.','[0.0195159912109375,0.0005950927734375,0.0016040802001953125,0.0279388427734375,0.06561279296875,0.04278564453125,0.039337158203125,0.046539306640625,-0.0131988525390625,-0.07354736328125,-0.0114288330078125,-0.0232391357421875,-0.0775146484375,0.02569580078125,-0.00913238525390625,0.053619384765625,0.07147216796875,-0.017547607421875,-0.0256500244140625,0.008026123046875,0.0322265625,-0.00226593017578125,-0.00943756103515625,0.0268402099609375,0.033905029296875,-0.007305145263671875,0.0307159423828125,0.01593017578125,-0.09814453125,-0.01486968994140625,0.0269317626953125,0.0237884521484375,-0.002445220947265625,-0.04278564453125,0.037353515625,