INSERT INTO city_chunks VALUES(82,'portland',4,'late rent payments, informal arrangements such as couch‑surfing, and eventual eviction. Losing a rental makes it much harder to secure another unit, especially with poor credit or an eviction record. ### FACTOR: Limited addiction and behavioral health resources - Type: service_gap - Content: There are not enough addiction treatment and behavioral health services to meet need. People with untreated mental health conditions or substance use disorders are at greater risk of homelessness and may struggle more to exit homelessness. ### NOTE: Limits of homelessness services department - Type: systems_context - Content: Some of the main drivers of homelessness in Portland—such as the housing market, inflation, and labor conditions—are largely outside the control of the homeless services department, even though that department responds to their impacts. # CITY GOVERNMENT POLICIES AND PROGRAMS (PORTLAND) ## POLICY: Mayor Wilson’s shelter expansion plan - Type: shelter_policy - Content: The mayor has proposed a large shelter expansion intended to provide enough beds for a majority of unsheltered people in the region. The plan includes a limit on length of stay (around three months) and aims to move people quickly through shelters.','[0.006343841552734375,-0.038970947265625,-0.01105499267578125,0.041107177734375,0.07098388671875,0.0181427001953125,0.0540771484375,0.02239990234375,-0.034454345703125,-0.047088623046875,-0.03363037109375,-0.006137847900390625,-0.060546875,0.02001953125,0.015655517578125,0.04046630859375,0.078369140625,-0.0264129638671875,0.0016622543334960938,-0.0083770751953125,0.0203857421875,0.0219879150390625,-0.002033233642578125,0.030242919921875,0.0234222412109375,-0.0088348388671875,-0.005207061767578125,-0.0128173828125,-0.0634765625,0.00035858154296875,0.041534423828125,0.0031757354736328125,-0.014312744140625,-0.0250701904296875,0.049041748046875,-0.016754150390625,-0.00572967529296875,0.00322723388671875